      "evidence": [],
      "notes": "docs/architecture/STORAGE_AND_DATA_PATHS.md + crates/sure-core/src/paths/{mod,compare}.rs; dirs 6.0.0 for OS-native known folders (SHGetKnownFolderPath needs unsafe, forbidden workspace-wide); data=%LOCALAPPDATA%\\SURE, config=%APPDATA%\\SURE asked separately; Paths::ensure_outside refuses a project root containing the store (home-directory case); Paths::from_roots refuses relative; compare.rs is component-wise, case-folds where the platform folds, and unifies \\?\\ canonical spellings; 40 tests in paths (Windows), clippy clean for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu and x86_64-apple-darwin; commit b6a14b4"
    },
    "P1-T005": {
      "status": "accepted",
      "started_at": "2026-09-14T09:37:44.399Z",
      "finished_at": "2026-09-14T10:03:35.856Z",
      "base_sha": null,
      "head_sha": null,
      "evidence": [],
      "notes": "SQLite compiled in (bundled), one STRICT table with AUTOINCREMENT, migrations through PRAGMA user_version with one transaction each and an in-transaction version re-read; records carry document_version and refuse to decode from a newer build. Gate set: fmt clean, clippy -D warnings clean, 408 passed / 0 failed, bootstrap 17 phases 166 tasks. Concurrency and packaging verified by tests/store_concurrency.rs (real child processes behind a barrier) and tests/store_packaging.rs (manifest-level). Two real bugs found by mutation-checking green tests: the journal-mode busy-handler exception (fixed by establish_journal_mode) and Store::write_error reporting DEFAULT_BUSY_TIMEOUT instead of the configured one. Commit 976d79a."
    },
    "P1-T006": {
      "status": "accepted",
      "started_at": null,
      "finished_at": "2026-09-14T09:17:16.123Z",
      "base_sha": null,
      "head_sha": null,
      "evidence": [],
      "notes": "crates/sure-core/src/diagnostics/{mod,correlation,field,time}.rs + docs/architecture/DIAGNOSTICS.md + ADR 0012 + redact moved to crate root; Correlation carries run always, session/check when known (unknown omitted, never a placeholder); RunId added as frozen kind 'run' (wire contract test updated, DOMAIN_SEMANTICS_VERSION not bumped - addition, not reinterpretation); message and field keys are &'static str; Field::text redacts on construction, discards by credential-shaped key, Field::redacted takes no value so no secret is ever required; values quoted so a value cannot restructure a line; no stdout sink exists; RFC 3339 UTC timestamps via civil_from_days tested against known instants; 133 sure-core lib tests pass, clippy -D warnings clean, cargo test --workspace green, cross-target clippy clean for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu and x86_64-apple-darwin; commit ad05ee1"
    },
    "P1-T007": {
      "status": "accepted",
      "started_at": "2026-09-14T09:17:19.460Z",
      "finished_at": "2026-09-14T09:37:13.253Z",
      "base_sha": null,
      "head_sha": null,
      "evidence": [],
      "notes": "crates/sure-protocol: schema.rs (hand-written validator for exactly the 11 keywords the schemas use; an unsupported keyword is a parse error rather than a silent skip, format:date-time is enforced rather than annotation-only, ANNOTATION_KEYWORDS names which keywords carry no constraint), documents.rs (DocumentKind registry with include_str! so an installed sure.exe validates against the schema its code was built from), event.rs (EventEnvelope, closed with deny_unknown_fields, numeric capability_tier, 4-step read: JSON syntax -> version -> schema -> serde). tests/conformance.rs (12) and tests/round_trip.rs (15). Found and fixed two real contract gaps that were invisible while only enum names were compared: RepairContract serialized its issue as 'issue' while repair.schema.json requires 'issue_id' (field renamed), and CheckResult carried neither evidence_class nor project_fingerprint (both now required, not_run/errored force Unknown). Also fixed a validator bug found by its own test: additionalProperties:false was checked inside the properties lookup, so a closed object with no properties allowed every key; a closed object with no properties now allows none, with a named regression test. Verified non-vacuous by mutation (renaming the domain field back to 'issue' fails 3 tests). New docs/architecture/PROTOCOL.md is the authority for the wire contract; FROZEN_SEMANTICS gap 1 struck through and its enforcement table extended. Gates: cargo fmt --check clean; clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings clean; cross-target clippy clean for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu and x86_64-apple-darwin; cargo test --workspace 341 passed / 0 failed (sure-protocol 39 lib + 12 conformance + 15 round_trip); node scripts/validate-bootstrap.mjs 17 phases / 166 tasks."
    },
